ould explain constitutional symptoms but lacks acute leukemic blast proliferation", "Diabetic complication syndrome: less likely to account for blasts or pancytopenia"], "alarm_features": ["Constitutional symptoms (fever, weight loss, night sweats)", "Pancytopenia with blasts on peripheral blood smear"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.04476139156395442, "posterior": 0.03461247409325737, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Marrow infiltration is more typical of myeloid neoplasms. Plasma cell disorders show minimal increase in likelihood due to low sensitivity of the finding."], "evidence_against": ["The absence of bone pain and B12 abnormalities reduces the likelihood of myeloid neoplasm, which typically presents with these features. This finding moderatel…"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.8, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute myeloid leukemia", "myelodysplastic syndrome with excess blasts", "chronic myeloid leukemia in blast crisis"]}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.39367760282841674, "posterior": 0.3799211745890024, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Marrow infiltration is more typical of myeloid neoplasms. Plasma cell disorders show minimal increase in likelihood due to low sensitivity of the finding."], "evidence_against": ["Lymphoid neoplasms rarely present with neurological deficits. This finding reduces the likelihood of lymphoid neoplasm but does not exclude it outright."], "unresolved_questions": [], "chi