ion, balance problems, bleeding from the gums, blurred vision, cellular immunodeficiency\n\nPlasma Cell Disorder vs Lymphoblastic Lymphoma:\n  Favours first:  abnormality of the bladder, abnormality of vitamin b12 metabolism, acute kidney injury, bone pain, decreased circulating antibody level\n  Favours second: autosomal dominant somatic cell mutation, cellular immunodeficiency, chronic lymphatic leukemia\n\nPlasma Cell Disorder vs Chronic Lymphocytic Leukemia (CLL) with Accelerated Phase / Transformation:\n  Favours first:  abnormality of the bladder, abnormality of vitamin b12 metabolism, acute kidney injury, decreased circulating antibody level, elevated serum creatinine\n  Favours second: abdominal pain or fullness, anemia, bleeding, easy bruising, fever\n\nPlasma Cell Disorder vs Polycythemia Vera:\n  Favours first:  abnormality of the bladder, abnormality of vitamin b12 metabolism, acute kidney injury, decreased circulating antibody level, elevated serum creatinine\n  Favours second: abdominal pain, abnormal erythrocyte morphology, bleeding gums, blurred vision, burning sensation in extremities\n\nPlasma Cell Disorder vs Essential Thrombocythemia:\n  Favours first:  abnormality of the bladder, abnormality of vitamin b12 metabolism, acute kidney injury, bone pain, decreased circulating antibody level\n  Favours second: abnormal cerebral vascular morphology, abnormal platelet morphology, abnormal thrombocyte morphology, abnormality of bone marrow cell morphology, amaurosis fugax\n\nPlasma Cell Disorder vs Primary Myelofibrosis:\n  Favours first:  abnormality of the bladder, abnormality of vitamin b12 metabolism, acute kidney injury, bone pain, decreased circulating antibody level\n  Favours second: abnormal bleeding, abnormal megakaryocyte morphology, abnormal thrombosis, abnormality of blood and blood-forming tissues, abnormality of bone marrow cell morphology\n\nDe Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia vs Chronic Myeloid Leukemia in Blast Crisis:\n  Favours first:  acute myeloid leukemia, autosomal dominant inheritance\n  Favours second: abdominal pain, abnormal basophil morphology, abnormal granulocyte morphology, abnormal/excessive bleeding, abnormality of blood and blood-forming tissues\n\nDe Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia vs Myelodysplastic Syndrome with Excess Blasts / Secondary AML:\n  Favours first:  autosomal dominant inheritance, somatic mutation\n  Favours second: abnormal bleeding, abnormal circulating albumin concentration, abnormal circulating protein concentration, abnormal mean corpuscular volume, abnormality of bone marrow cell morphology\n\nDe Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia vs De Novo Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia (ALL):\n  Favours first:  acute myeloid leukemia, autosomal dominant inheritance\n  Favours second: autosomal dominant somatic cell mutation, balance problems, bleeding from the gums, blurred vision, bone pain\n\nDe Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia vs Lymphoblastic Lymphoma:\n  Favours first:  acute myeloid leukemia, autosomal dominant inheritance\n  Favours second: autosomal dominant somatic cell mutation, cellular immunodeficiency, chronic lymphatic leukemia"}
